---
import Icon from './Icon.astro';

const editors = ['VS Code', 'Neovim', 'Vim', 'JetBrains', 'Zed'];
---

<section class="section benefits" id="benefits" aria-labelledby="benefits-title">
  <div class="shell">
    <div class="section-head reveal">
      <p class="eyebrow">Why it works</p>
      <h2 id="benefits-title" class="section-title">Shadow moves files, not pixels</h2>
      <p class="section-lead">
        It watches your project folder and syncs every change to your partner’s copy.
        Because it works under the editor, nobody has to agree on one.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="bento">
      <article class="tile tile-wide reveal">
        <div class="tile-icon"><Icon name="code" /></div>
        <h3>Keep your editor, keymap, and extensions</h3>
        <p>
          Your partner’s Vim config never touches your setup. Each of you edits real files on your own disk,
          with your own linters, debugger, and terminal.
        </p>
        <ul class="editor-chips" role="list" aria-label="Editors people pair from">
          {editors.map((e) => <li>{e}</li>)}
          <li class="is-more">anything that saves files</li>
        </ul>
      </article>

      <article class="tile reveal reveal-d1">
        <div class="tile-icon"><Icon name="lightning" /></div>
        <h3>Both of you type, live</h3>
        <p>
          No driver, no passenger. Shadow picks up each save after a 50 ms debounce and checks it by hash,
          so unchanged files are never resent.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="tile reveal">
        <div class="tile-icon"><Icon name="user-circle-dashed" /></div>
        <h3>Nothing to sign up for</h3>
        <p>
          No email, no OAuth, no workspace invite. Shadow opens a secure tunnel for you and copies the
          invite link. Your partner needs the link and nothing else.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="tile reveal reveal-d1">
        <div class="tile-icon"><Icon name="eye" /></div>
        <h3>Read only when you want it</h3>
        <p>
          Running an interview or a review? Turn on “Joiners are read only” in the app,
          or pass <code class="inline-code">--read-only-joiners</code>, and they watch without editing.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="tile reveal reveal-d2">
        <div class="tile-icon"><Icon name="shield-check" /></div>
        <h3>Guardrails against oversharing</h3>
        <p>
          Shadow refuses to share system folders like your home directory,
          respects <code class="inline-code">.gitignore</code>, and skips <code class="inline-code">.git</code>
          and <code class="inline-code">node_modules</code>.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .bento {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: var(--sp-200);
  }

  .tile {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--sp-100);
    padding: var(--sp-400);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: var(--r-2xl);
    background: var(--surface);
    transition: border-color var(--dur-fast) var(--ease);
  }

  .tile:hover {
    border-color: var(--border-strong);
  }

  .tile-wide {
    grid-column: 1 / -1;
  }

  .tile-icon {
    display: grid;
    place-items: center;
    width: 40px;
    height: 40px;
    margin-bottom: var(--sp-100);
    border-radius: var(--r-lg);
    background: var(--accent-soft);
    color: var(--accent);
  }

  .tile h3 {
    font-size: var(--text-xl);
    line-height: var(--lh-xl);
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
    color: var(--text);
  }

  .tile p {
    max-width: 640px;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
  }

  .editor-chips {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: var(--sp-75);
    margin-top: var(--sp-200);
    list-style: none;
  }

  .editor-chips li {
    padding: var(--sp-50) var(--sp-100);
    border: 1px solid var(--border-strong);
    border-radius: var(--r-full);
    background: var(--surface-raised);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--text-xs);
    line-height: var(--lh-xs);
    color: var(--text);
  }

  .editor-chips .is-more {
    border-style: dashed;
    background: transparent;
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }

  @media (max-width: 767px) {
    .bento {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }

    .tile {
      padding: var(--sp-300);
    }
  }
</style>
